lagfinder.tip.alloc_jfr=Java's Flight Recorder took samples of the objects created, each with its type and where it was created; each stands for the bytes allocated since the one before, so the bytes add up to about all that was allocated. It costs very little.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_stacks=This Java has no Flight Recorder (Java 16 or later is needed). The scanned thread's stack was sampled instead, with the bytes it allocated in between: who allocates is known roughly, what type of objects is not.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_share=Share
